      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just walking through the logic for this \"out loud\".\n- This block is wrapped in `#ifdef CHIP_FAMILY_STM32F0` from [line 334]( https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/refs/changes/69/3656369/7/chip/stm32/dma.c#334), so it only applies to stm32f0\n- For stm32f0, `STM32_DMAC_COUNT` is defined as [7 on line 719 of registers-stm32f0.h](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h;l\u003d719) or [5 on line 722 of registers-stm32f0.h](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h;l\u003d722). \n- The value depends upon this condition from [line 708 of registers-stm32f0.h](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h;l\u003d708): \n`#if !defined(CHIP_VARIANT_STM32F03X) \u0026\u0026 !defined(CHIP_VARIANT_STM32F05X)`\n- The names of DMAC channels are set to [one more than their actual values](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/chip/stm32/registers-stm32f0.h;l\u003d680) (i.e. `STM32_MAC_CH4` has a value of 4), and `STM32_DMAC_COUNT` is intended to represent the number of channels, not the highest channel number.\n- For the 7 channel DMA: This function should execute on channels `STM32_DMAC4`, `STM32_DMAC5`, `STM32_DMAC6`, and `STM32_DMAC7` (with integer values of 3, 4, 5, and 6). The loop starts at `STM32_DMAC4` (3) and should end after `STM32_DMAC7` (6). This all seems correct.\n- For the 5 channel DMA, this function should execute on channels `STM32_DMAC4`, `STM32_DMAC5` (with integer values of 3 and 4). The loop starts at `STM32_DMAC4` (3) and should end `STM32_DMAC5` (4). This all seems correct.",
      "revId": "f4dfe7ecdf67e4d0b2f6dc7829d86531f6b4d9a4",
